  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <h3>Why are you moving to Australia?</h3>
  <p>
    In January 2017 I flew to Byron Bay for my chef apprenticeship, Lucy followed in February for her semester abroad. One semester became two, almost two years in the region in which we felt at home. Since returning to Germany at the end of 2018 the wish to go back never fully went away, but for years it stayed a pipe dream without serious ambition. In 2026, Lucy's Master's degree, Joris starting school and our restaurant fatigue all lined up at the same point.
  </p>

  <h3>What was the concrete trigger for the decision?</h3>
  <p>
    In early September 2025 we had to clear our second vegetable field. Again a lot of work that wasn't rewarded, again a plan that didn't work out. In that moment the doubts about the restaurant and the old Australia idea flowed together: now or never. The decision to close the restaurant and the decision to emigrate were made together, not one after the other.
  </p>

  <h3>When did you close die farm?</h3>
  <p>
    We ran die farm, our restaurant in Essen, from 1 February 2019 to 31 December 2025, almost seven years. In October 2025 we celebrated our own wedding there, two months before closing. Our team was loyal and well-rehearsed, staff shortages were not a closure factor. Emigration was.
  </p>

  <h3>How did you find a sponsoring employer as a chef in Australia?</h3>
  <p>
    Not online, but on the ground. The tip from the German expat meetup in Byron Bay: walk around, be open, talk to people, hospitality is always hiring. That's exactly how it went. I walked into restaurants in person and introduced myself. In the end we found each other with <a href="https://www.threeways.store/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Threeways of the Valley</a>, a cafe-restaurant in the Byron Bay hinterland rainforest. After many evenings talking about plans and visions, the team there is now working on their part of my 186 application, the nomination.
  </p>

  <h3>Why did Christian fly alone first?</h3>
  <p>
    I flew ahead on 23 June 2026, Lucy and the kids landed in Brisbane on 28 July. In the five weeks in between I sorted sponsor, car and accommodation: a job perspective with a sponsorship commitment, a Jeep for 4,500 AUD, two housesits and an Airbnb as a bridge. When the three of them arrived, the frame was in place. That was exactly the plan, and it worked.
  </p>

  <h3>What does it cost to move to Australia as a family?</h3>
  <p>
    By early May 2026 we had spent around 6,900 € on preparation in Germany, the biggest item being the family flights. The 186 visa application fees for four people were raised on 1 July 2026 to roughly 12,280 AUD (previously roughly 9,825 AUD). For the start in Australia we had a 30,000 AUD reserve. The full breakdown, paid and estimated, is in our cost article: <a href="/en/cost-of-moving-to-australia-family-guide">Cost of Moving to Australia as a Family</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Do you regret emigrating?</h3>
  <p>
    One week into being a family of four here, it is too early for that question. Right now we have a very good feeling, it feels right. We are honest about it: this is not everyday life yet, it feels more like a holiday. The distance to our families in Germany is hard, daily video calls make it okay. If the visa doesn't work out, we fly back, that has been part of the plan from the start.
  </p>

  <h3>Which visa are you using, and what is the status?</h3>
  <p>
    We all entered on the free eVisitor (subclass 651). The goal is the permanent 186 visa (Employer Nomination Scheme). It is a two-stage process: first the employer lodges the nomination, then I lodge my visa application, supported by <a href="https://jkmigrate.com.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Johannes Kunz</a>. The nomination is currently in progress. After the 186 application the whole family receives a bridging visa; the eVisitor carries no no-further-stay condition. We describe the whole route here: <a href="/en/186-visa-australia-family-guide">186 Visa Australia</a>.
  </p>

